<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Wikipedia - Web Development</title>
    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #202122;
            background: #fff;
        }

        header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 20px;
            padding: 18px 30px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
        }

        .logo {
            font-family: Georgia, serif;
            font-size: 32px;
        }

        .search {
            flex: 1;
            max-width: 500px;
            padding: 9px;
            border: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
        }

        .layout {
            display: flex;
            max-width: 1250px;
            margin: auto;
        }

        aside {
            width: 230px;
            padding: 25px 20px;
            border-right: 1px solid #eaecf0;
        }

        aside h3 {
            font-size: 15px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecf0;
            padding-bottom: 8px;
        }

        aside a {
            display: block;
            margin: 12px 0;
            color: #36c;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        main {
            flex: 1;
            padding: 25px 35px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-family: Georgia, serif;
            font-size: 34px;
            font-weight: normal;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }

        h2 {
            font-family: Georgia, serif;
            font-weight: normal;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
            padding-bottom: 6px;
        }

        p {
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        a {
            color: #36c;
        }

        .infobox {
            float: right;
            width: 280px;
            margin: 0 0 20px 25px;
            padding: 10px;
            background: #f8f9fa;
            border: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
        }

        .infobox h3 {
            text-align: center;
            background: #dbeafe;
            padding: 10px;
            margin-top: 0;
        }

        .infobox img {
            width: 100%;
            height: 130px;
            object-fit: cover;
            background: #ddd;
        }

        .infobox td {
            padding: 7px;
            border-top: 1px solid #c8ccd1;
            vertical-align: top;
        }

        footer {
            margin-top: 30px;
            padding: 20px;
            border-top: 1px solid #a2a9b1;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #54595d;
        }

        @media (max-width: 700px) {
            .layout {
                display: block;
            }

            aside {
                width: 100%;
                border-right: 0;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecf0;
            }

            .infobox {
                float: none;
                width: 100%;
                margin: 15px 0;
            }

            main {
                padding: 20px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <div class="logo">WIKIPEDIA</div>
        <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="Search Wikipedia">
        <a href="#">Log in</a>
    </header>

    <div class="layout">
        <aside>
            <h3>Contents</h3>
            <a href="#introduction">Introduction</a>
            <a href="#history">History</a>
            <a href="#technologies">Technologies</a>
            <a href="#importance">Importance</a>
            <a href="#references">References</a>
        </aside>

        <main>
            <div class="infobox">
                <h3>Web development</h3>
                <div style="height:130px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
                    🌐
                </div>
                <table>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Type</strong></td>
                        <td>Software development</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
                        <td>Creating websites and applications</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Common tools</strong></td>
                        <td>HTML, CSS, JavaScript</td>
                    </tr>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h1>Web development</h1>
            <p><em>From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</em></p>

            <p>
                <strong>Web development</strong> is the process of creating and maintaining
                websites and web applications. It involves design, programming, databases,
                security, and server management.
            </p>

            <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                Web developers use a combination of technologies to build pages that can be
                viewed in a web browser. Websites may be simple collections of documents or
                complex applications that provide interactive services.
            </p>

            <h2 id="history">History</h2>
            <p>
                The modern web began as a system for sharing documents over the Internet.
                Over time, it developed into a platform supporting communication, education,
                commerce, entertainment, and many other activities.
            </p>

            <h2 id="technologies">Technologies</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>HTML</strong> defines the structure of a webpage.</li>
                <li><strong>CSS</strong> controls its appearance and layout.</li>
                <li><strong>JavaScript</strong> adds interactivity and dynamic behavior.</li>
                <li><strong>Servers and databases</strong> store and deliver information.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="importance">Importance</h2>
            <p>
                Web development enables organizations and individuals to publish information,
                provide online services, and connect with users around the world.
            </p>

            <h2 id="references">References</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><a href="#">Introduction to web technologies</a></li>
                <li><a href="#">World Wide Web standards</a></li>
            </ol>
        </main>
    </div>

    <footer>
        This page is a fictional Wikipedia-style example created for learning HTML and CSS.
    </footer>
</body>
</html>